Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 08:55:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] duck-brain P7: robot.say plays a synthesised phrase from
 [audio] say_dir
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The duck speaks (duck-brain design §21): its duck-say writes a wav into
/run/duck-say and asks robotd to play it, through the same single-client
PCM as the bank sounds (sound.rs: one playing child, a new sound cuts it).
Only a .wav inside say_dir, resolved, is played; audio off refuses. btd
refuses it over the radio; updater routes it with the other robot.* calls.
